<article class="env-lemma" id="00QY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00QY">Lemma <span data-tag="00QY">10.127.14</span>.</a> Suppose $R \to S$ is a ring map. Then there exists a directed set $(\Lambda , \leq )$, and a system of ring maps $R_\lambda \to S_\lambda $ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The colimit of the system $R_\lambda \to S_\lambda $ is equal to $R \to S$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Each $R_\lambda $ is of finite type over $\mathbf{Z}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Each $S_\lambda $ is of finite type over $R_\lambda $. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is the non-local version of Lemma <a href="/tag/00QT" data-tag="00QT">10.127.9</a>. Proof is similar and left to the reader. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>